en, took place from 17 to 20 May 2018 at Rinkven International Golf Club, Schilde, Antwerp. In the final, the Spaniard Adrián Otaegui won against Frenchman Benjamin Hébert after four match days. David Drysdale took third place after winning against James Heath. In 1957 Hunt (137) beat Rees (145) by 8 strokes in a 36-hole playoff. In 1935 Branch (145) beat Van Donck (149) by 4 strokes in a 36-hole playoff.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d01\", \"text\": \"Belgian Open (tennis) The Belgian Open was a WTA Tour tennis event held over three different periods during 1987–2002. The competition took place in July during 1987–1989 and 2002, and in May during 1992–1993 and 1999–2001. During 2000–2001 it was sponsored by Dutch clothing chain Mexx and renamed the \\\"Benelux Open\\\". The competition was played on outdoor clay courts. The tournament was a Tier V event in 1992 and 2001. The tournament was a Tier IV event in 1993, 1999, 2000 and 2002. Only one Belgian woman won the singles event; the then little-known Justine Henin, aged 16 in 1999.\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"Tennis\", \"Squash\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"The Belgian Open is primarily associated with tennis. It has also been a major squash tournament. Uncertainty exists regarding which specific sport the user intends without further context.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Belgian Open\", \"scope\": \"Sport association\", \"claim\": \"The Belgian Open is a golf tournament, as evidenced by its 2018 edition taking place at Rinkven International Golf Club and historical references to 36-hole playoffs and stroke counts.\", \"answer\": \"Golf\", \"quote\": \"to the European Tour. The Belgian Open was reintroduced under the name Belgian Knockout. The first edition of the Belgian Knockout, which is the 53rd edition of the Belgian Open, took place from 17 to 20 May 2018 at Rinkven International Golf Club, Schilde, Antwerp. In the final, the Spaniard Adrián Otaegui won against Frenchman Benjamin Hébert after four match days. David Drysdale took third place after winning against James Heath. In 1957 Hunt (137) beat Rees (145) by 8 strokes in a 36-hole playoff. In 1935 Branch (145) beat Van Donck (149) by 4 strokes in a 36-hole playoff.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0217-3ad756dbc3cb:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Belgian Open\", \"scope\": \"sport association\", \"claim\": \"The Belgian Open was a WTA Tour tennis event.\", \"answer\": \"tennis\", \"quote\": \"Belgian Open (tennis) The Belgian Open was a WTA Tour tennis event held over three different periods during 1987–2002.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"fallible_previous_answer\": [\"Golf\", \"Tennis\"]}"
